          Example: `10 Gbps`
        type: string
      peeringLocation:
        description: The provider's peering location.
        maxLength: 255
        minLength: 1
        type: string
    required:
      - name
  FlowLogConfig:
    description: |
      *Flow logs* record information about traffic that is either allowed or rejected by the
      [security lists](#/en/iaas/latest/SecurityList/) that control traffic in and out of a
      [VNIC](#/en/iaas/latest/Vnic/).

      A *flow log configuration* (`FlowLogConfig`) contains information about where to store flow
      logs (an Object Storage bucket in your tenancy), and the type of logs to store.

      **Important:** For logs to be placed in the Object Storage bucket listed in the configuration,
      an administrator must create an IAM policy in your tenancy that lets the Networking service
      put objects in that bucket. Otherwise, no flow logs can be written to the bucket.
      Here's the required policy (which consists of three separate statements):

      `define tenancy VcnFlowLogs as ocid1.tenancy.oc1..<var>&lt;unique_ID&gt;</var>`

      `define dynamic-group FlowLogsDynamicGroup as ocid1.dynamicgroup.oc1..<var>&lt;unique_ID&gt;</var>`

      `admit dynamic-group FlowLogsDynamicGroup of tenancy VcnFlowLogs to manage objects in tenancy where target.bucket.name='yourbucketname'`

      To enable flow logs for a subnet: after creating a flow
      log configuration, attach the flow log configuration to that subnet. See
      [FlowLogConfigAttachment](#/en/iaas/latest/FlowLogConfigAttachment/) and
      [CreateFlowLogConfigAttachment](#/en/iaas/latest/FlowLogConfigAttachment/CreateFlowLogConfigAttachment).

    x-obmcs-splat:
      resourceKind: flowlogconfig
      adLocality: regional
    properties:
      compartmentId:
        description: |
          The [OCID](/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm) of the compartment containing the flow
          log configuration.
        maxLength: 255
        minLength: 1
        type: string
      definedTags: *ref-definedTags
      displayName: *ref-displayName
      freeformTags: *ref-freeformTags
      id:
        description: The flow log configuration's [OCID](/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm).
        maxLength: 255
        minLength: 1
        type: string
      lifecycleState:
        description: The flow log configuration's current state.
        enum:
          - PROVISIONING
          - AVAILABLE
          - TERMINATING
          - TERMINATED
        type: string
      flowLogType:
        description: |
          Type or types of flow logs to store. `ALL` includes records for both accepted traffic and
          rejected traffic.
        enum:
          - ALL
        type: string
      destination:
        $ref: '#/definitions/FlowLogDestination'
      timeCreated:
        description: |
          The date and time the flow log configuration was created, in the format defined by [RFC3339](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339).

          Example: `2016-08-25T21:10:29.600Z`
        format: date-time
        type: string
    required:
      - compartmentId
      - displayName
      - id
      - lifecycleState
      - flowLogType
      - destination
      - timeCreated
  FlowLogConfigAttachment:
    description: |
      Represents an attachment between a flow log configuration and a resource such as a subnet. By
      creating a `FlowLogConfigAttachment`, you turn on flow logs for the attached resource. See
      [CreateFlowLogConfigAttachment](#/en/iaas/latest/FlowLogConfigAttachment/CreateFlowLogConfigAttachment).

    x-obmcs-splat:
      resourceKind: flowlogconfigattachment
      adLocality: regional
    properties:
      compartmentId:
        description: |
          The [OCID](/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm) of the compartment containing the
          flow log configuration attachment.
        maxLength: 255
        minLength: 1
        type: string
      displayName: *ref-displayName
      id:
        description: The flow log configuration attachment's [OCID](/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm).
        maxLength: 255
        minLength: 1
        type: string
      lifecycleState:
        description: The flow log configuration attachment's current state.
        enum:
          - PROVISIONING
          - AVAILABLE
          - TERMINATING
          - TERMINATED
        type: string
      targetEntityId:
        description: |
          The [OCID](/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm) of the resource that the flow log
          configuration is attached to.
        maxLength: 255
        minLength: 1
        type: string
      targetEntityType:
        description: |
          The type of resource that the flow log configuration is attached to.
        enum:
          - SUBNET
        type: string
      flowLogConfigId:
        description: |
          The [OCID](/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm) of the flow log configuration that
          is attached to the resource.
        maxLength: 255
        minLength: 1
        type: string
      timeCreated:
        description: |
          The date and time the flow log configuration attachment was created, in the format defined by [RFC3339](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339).

          Example: `2016-08-25T21:10:29.600Z`
        format: date-time
        type: string
    required:
      - compartmentId
      - displayName
      - id
      - lifecycleState
      - targetEntityId
      - targetEntityType
      - flowLogConfigId
      - timeCreated
  FlowLogDestination:
    description: |
      Where to store the flow logs.
    discriminator: destinationType
    properties:
      destinationType:
        description: |
          Type of location for storing flow logs.
        enum:
          - OBJECT_STORAGE
        type: string
    required:
      - destinationType
